<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Bottom-nav item press state (GH #170 / FRM-131).

     DESIGN-SYSTEM-PHASE3.md 6.1 specifies press feedback as "a Material
     ripple at 12% fm_primary, nothing else" - 12% of 255 is ~31 (0x1F),
     matching bg_home_row_ripple.xml. The bar previously set no
     itemBackground or itemRippleColor at all, so it inherited the stock M3
     ripple rather than this token.

     The mask is what fixes the reported symptom. The item's background
     bounds are 137 x 64dp (measured: a zero-inset oval mask renders exactly
     137.0 x 63.6dp). An unmasked ripple therefore grows as a circle only
     until it reaches 64dp tall, then keeps widening to the full 137dp -
     measured 37x37 -> 67x63 -> 91x64 -> 137x64. That flattening is what GH
     #170 describes as "clipped by the navbar frame".

     48dp is not arbitrary and must not be "rounded up":
       - It is DESIGN-SYSTEM-PHASE3.md 6.2's icon-button target.
       - It is the largest value that actually works here. Measured on
         device, 56dp and 64dp masks FAIL: RippleDrawable silently discards
         the mask and falls back to the unmasked full-bounds ripple
         (137 x 83dp and 137 x 87dp respectively), i.e. the original bug,
         worse. Only 48dp renders as a true circle.
       - At 48dp the ripple measures 47.6 x 47.6dp centred at 32.2dp from
         the bar top, against a glyph centre of 32.0dp - centred on the
         glyph, and circular for the whole expansion.

     gravity="center" is correct because the background bounds are the 64dp
     content area, whose centre already coincides with the glyph centre. Do
     not add an android:top offset: the 72dp figure uiautomator reports for
     the item node is the node's bounds, not this drawable's. -->
<ripple xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:color="#1F1F817D">
    <item android:id="@android:id/mask">
        <layer-list>
            <item
                android:width="48dp"
                android:height="48dp"
                android:gravity="center">
                <shape android:shape="oval">
                    <solid android:color="#FFFFFFFF" />
                </shape>
            </item>
        </layer-list>
    </item>
</ripple>
